---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import sketch from '../assets/login-sketch.svg?raw';
---

<Layout
	title="wiremark — text-based, markdown-embeddable wireframes"
	description="wiremark is a concise, agent-friendly wireframing DSL inspired by YAML's simplicity and MUI's readability. Embed it in markdown or write standalone files; it renders as a hand-drawn sketch."
>
	<!-- ---- hero ---- -->
	<section class="hero">
		<img
			class="hero-logo"
			src="/wiremark-icon.svg"
			alt=""
			width="314"
			height="176"
		/>
		<h1>wiremark</h1>
		<p class="tagline">A text-based, markdown-embeddable wireframing format</p>
		<p class="lede">
			Inspired by <strong>YAML’s simplicity</strong> and
			<strong><a href="https://mui.com/">MUI</a>’s readability</strong> —
			a concise, agent-friendly, easy-to-read DSL for wireframes, rendered in
			a hand-drawn, Balsamiq-like style. Embed it in markdown files the way
			Mermaid does, or write it as standalone <code>.wiremark</code> files.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-actions">
			<a class="button button-primary" href="https://docs.wiremark.dev/guides/introduction">
				Read the docs
			</a>
			<a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/Blackburn-Labs/wiremark">
				GitHub
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ---- demo: source -> sketch ---- -->
	<section class="demo">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="demo-grid">
				<div class="demo-source">
					<div class="demo-label">Write this in any markdown file…</div>
					<pre
						class="demo-code"><code><span class="tok-fence">```wireframe</span>
<span class="tok-component">Wireframe</span> <span class="tok-attr">mobile</span>
  <span class="tok-component">Stack</span> <span class="tok-attr">col</span> <span class="tok-attr">gap=2</span>
    <span class="tok-component">Typography</span> <span class="tok-attr">h4</span> <span class="tok-string">"Sign in"</span>
    <span class="tok-component">TextField</span> <span class="tok-string">"Email"</span>
    <span class="tok-component">TextField</span> <span class="tok-string">"Password"</span>
    <span class="tok-component">Button</span> <span class="tok-string">"Sign in"</span> <span class="tok-attr">primary</span>
<span class="tok-fence">```</span></code></pre>
				</div>
				<div class="demo-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
				<div class="demo-render">
					<div class="demo-label">…and get this</div>
					<div class="demo-sketch" set:html={sketch} />
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="demo-caption">
				That block describes a phone-sized sign-in screen: a heading, two
				fields, and a primary button. No coordinates, no styling, no
				boilerplate — just the structure.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ---- mental model ---- -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>The whole format is three ideas</h2>
			<div class="cards cards-3">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Component names are MUI names</h3>
					<p>
						<code>Stack</code>, <code>Box</code>, <code>Typography</code>,
						<code>Card</code>, <code>Grid</code>, <code>Button</code>,
						<code>TextField</code>, <code>AppBar</code>, <code>List</code>, …
						If you would reach for a component in Material UI, reach for the
						same name here.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Indentation is containment</h3>
					<p>
						A line indented under another line is its child. That single rule
						replaces every wrapper, brace, and closing tag — the shape of the
						text <em>is</em> the shape of the screen.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Defaults do the work</h3>
					<p>
						A bare component name renders something sensible. A lone
						<code>Typography</code> is a line of placeholder text; a lone
						<code>Button</code> reads “Button”. You add detail only where it
						communicates something.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ---- key ideas ---- -->
	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Built to live in your documents</h2>
			<div class="cards cards-4">
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Markdown-native</h3>
					<p>
						A wireframe is a fenced code block, so it travels with your specs,
						PRDs, READMEs, and design notes — and renders inline via thin host
						adapters (Obsidian, markdown-it, remark, …) over one pure core.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Flow for free</h3>
					<p>
						Frames are named with <code>#id</code> and linked with
						<code>to=#id</code>, so an embedded navigation graph falls out of
						the document automatically.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Agent-first</h3>
					<p>
						Intentionally low-ambiguity and low-token. An LLM can read, write,
						and reason about a wireframe with no reference doc, leaning on what
						it already knows about MUI.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature">
					<h3>Hand-drawn by default</h3>
					<p>
						Output is a deliberate sketch, not a polished mockup. A sketch
						invites feedback on structure instead of bikeshedding on colors.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ---- packages ---- -->
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Get wiremark</h2>
			<div class="cards cards-2">
				<div class="card package">
					<h3>
						<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@wiremark/core">@wiremark/core</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						The parser, layout engine, and hand-drawn SVG renderer behind
						everything. Pure JS, no host dependencies.
					</p>
					<pre class="install"><code>npm install @wiremark/core</code></pre>
				</div>
				<div class="card package">
					<h3>
						<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@wiremark/cli">@wiremark/cli</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						The command-line renderer — turn a <code>.wiremark</code> file into
						an SVG without writing any code.
					</p>
					<pre class="install"><code>npx @wiremark/cli in.wiremark -o out.svg</code></pre>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="packages-note">
				MIT licensed. wiremark is young — the format is specified at v0.1 and
				the renderer is under active development. Follow along on
				<a href="https://github.com/Blackburn-Labs/wiremark">GitHub</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.container {
		max-width: 1140px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 1rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.75rem;
		line-height: 1.25;
		margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
		text-align: center;
	}

	/* ---- hero ---- */
	.hero {
		padding: 4.5rem 1rem 3.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		/* faint dot-grid, like sketching paper */
		background-image: radial-gradient(var(--color-border-subtle) 1px, transparent 1px);
		background-size: 24px 24px;
	}

	.hero-logo {
		height: 11rem;
		width: auto;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		font-size: 3.25rem;
		line-height: 1.1;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.tagline {
		font-size: 1.375rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin: 0 auto 1rem;
	}

	.lede {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: 1.0625rem;
	}

	.hero-actions {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.button {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid transparent;
	}

	.button:hover {
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.button-primary {
		background-color: var(--color-primary);
		border-color: var(--color-primary);
		color: #fff;
	}

	[data-theme='dark'] .button-primary {
		color: #1b1b1d;
	}

	.button-primary:hover {
		background-color: var(--color-primary-dark);
		border-color: var(--color-primary-dark);
	}

	.button-outline {
		border-color: var(--color-border);
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.button-outline:hover {
		background-color: var(--color-hover-overlay);
	}

	/* ---- demo ---- */
	.demo {
		padding: 3rem 0 1rem;
	}

	.demo-grid {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: stretch;
		gap: 1.75rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.demo-label {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}

	/* center the short code box against the tall phone sketch */
	.demo-source {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		min-width: 0;
		max-width: 100%;
	}

	.demo-render {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.demo-source .demo-code {
		margin: auto 0;
	}

	.demo-arrow {
		align-self: center;
		font-size: 2rem;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	.demo-code {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 100%;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background-color: var(--demo-code-bg);
		color: var(--demo-code-text);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		overflow-x: auto;
	}

	[data-theme='dark'] .demo-code {
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
	}

	/* the global inline-code chip style doesn't apply inside the demo block */
	.demo-code code {
		background: none;
		border: 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: inherit;
	}

	.tok-fence { color: var(--tok-fence); }
	.tok-component { color: var(--tok-component); }
	.tok-anchor { color: var(--tok-anchor); }
	.tok-attr { color: var(--tok-attr); }
	.tok-string { color: var(--tok-string); }

	.demo-sketch {
		background-color: #fff;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
		padding: 0.75rem;
		transform: rotate(-0.4deg);
	}

	.demo-sketch :global(svg) {
		display: block;
		width: auto;
		height: 440px;
	}

	.demo-caption {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 2rem auto 0;
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	/* ---- sections ---- */
	.section {
		padding: 3.5rem 0;
	}

	.section-alt {
		background-color: var(--color-surface);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
	}

	[data-theme='dark'] .section-alt {
		background-color: #1f2022;
	}

	.cards {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	/* minmax(0, …) so a wide <pre> can't push the track past the viewport */
	.cards-2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
	.cards-3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
	.cards-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }

	.card {
		background-color: var(--color-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		border-radius: calc(var(--radius) * 2);
		box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.card h3,
	.feature h3 {
		font-size: 1.0625rem;
		line-height: 1.3;
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
	}

	.card p,
	.feature p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	.feature h3 {
		color: var(--color-primary);
	}

	/* ---- packages ---- */
	.package h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}

	.package p {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.install {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
		background-color: var(--color-code-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		overflow-x: auto;
	}

	.install code {
		background: none;
		border: 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
	}

	.packages-note {
		margin: 2rem auto 0;
		max-width: 44rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	/* ---- responsive ---- */
	@media (max-width: 996px) {
		.cards-3,
		.cards-4 {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 2.5rem;
		}

		.tagline {
			font-size: 1.125rem;
		}

		.cards-2,
		.cards-3,
		.cards-4 {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}

		.demo-arrow {
			transform: rotate(90deg);
		}

		.demo-sketch :global(svg) {
			height: 380px;
		}
	}
</style>
